  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.2\n      - The .nuspec now declares the repository, which is public, and SourceLink is on: consumers can step into the source while debugging\n      - Support moves to GitHub issues now that the repository is public\n      - Microsoft.JSInterop and Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions move from 10.0.9 to 10.0.11\n      - The version history no longer lists a 1.0.2 that was never published: those changes shipped in 1.1.0\n      - No change to the code or to the public surface\n\n      v1.1.1\n      - Disposing the service while its first call is still importing no longer leaks the module reference\n      - The internal import gate is no longer disposed, so a call in flight does not fail on the way out\n      - A call that outlives its service is logged as Debug, not as an error\n      - The constructors document the exceptions they throw\n      - Corrects the README examples, which were missing a using directive and did not compile\n\n      v1.1.0\n      - Fixes the packaged wasmModuleLoader.js, which shipped truncated and could not be imported\n      - A failed module import is no longer cached: the next call retries instead of leaving the service dead\n      - Failures during the import are logged and swallowed, as the contract always promised\n      - DisposeAsync tolerates a torn-down circuit (JSDisconnectedException)\n      - One structured log entry per failure, carrying the exception and the method name\n      - WasmLoaderServiceBase is abstract, derives from JSLoaderServiceBase and takes a plain ILogger\n      - The dependency narrows to Microsoft.JSInterop and Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions",
